### @BookOwner  ->  BookStockServiceImpl#updateBookStock, guarded by BookOwnerAspect.
### This is the only new annotation with an observable HTTP effect: the owner gets 200,
### a non-owner gets 403 (UserNotAllowedException -> @ResponseStatus FORBIDDEN).
###
### Seeded books have creator_id = 'admin' (DB default), so:
###   - admin  owns seeded book 1            -> 200
###   - vova   is ADMIN but NOT the owner     -> 403  (this isolates @BookOwner from the
###            @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')") check, which vova passes)
###   - vova   owns a book he created himself -> 200
###
### Self-contained: it fetches the tokens it needs first.

### login admin
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/uni-book-store/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=uni-book-store-client&username=admin&password=admin

> {% client.global.set("admin_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### login vova
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/uni-book-store/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=uni-book-store-client&username=vova&password=vova

> {% client.global.set("vova_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 1) OWNER (admin) updates stock of seeded book 1 -> expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/v1/books/1/stock
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 25,
  "price": 19.99
}

> {%
    client.test("owner is allowed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 2) NON-OWNER (vova, also ADMIN) updates stock of seeded book 1 -> expect 403
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/v1/books/1/stock
Authorization: Bearer {{vova_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 10,
  "price": 9.99
}

> {%
    client.test("non-owner is forbidden by @BookOwner", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 403, "Expected 403 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 3) vova creates his own book (he becomes the creator/owner) -> expect 201
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/books
Authorization: Bearer {{vova_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Vova's Book",
  "description": "A book owned by vova",
  "author": "Vova",
  "genre": "FANTASY",
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/cover.jpg",
  "enabled": true,
  "price": 12.50,
  "quantity": 5
}

> {%
    client.test("vova created a book", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201 but got " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.id, "No book id in response");
    });
    client.global.set("vova_book_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 4) OWNER (vova) updates stock of the book he just created -> expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/v1/books/{{vova_book_id}}/stock
Authorization: Bearer {{vova_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 7,
  "price": 15.00
}

> {%
    client.test("creator may update own book stock", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}
